PART 11: CUSTOMER CASHBACK AND BONUS REDEMPTION

Customers should be able to use their available cashback and bonus balances whenever they make an eligible payment on Swiftvero.

This is an important requirement.

Do not make customers wait for a special campaign or contact Customer Service before using available rewards.

Integrate the existing cashback and bonus systems into the payment and checkout process.

Checkout behaviour

When a customer reaches the payment stage, show available rewards and allow them to choose how much of their eligible balance to apply.

For example:

* Shipping charge: ₦120,000.
* Available account credit: ₦10,000.
* Available cashback: ₦5,000.
* Available bonus: ₦5,000.
* Remaining amount payable: ₦100,000.

The customer should be able to select which balances to use.

Where the existing reward policy allows it, permit the customer to use cashback and bonuses together.

Do not force the customer to use all available rewards.

Allow partial redemption.

Clearly show:

* Original shipping charge.
* Account credit applied.
* Cashback applied.
* Bonus applied.
* Remaining amount to pay.

Reward restrictions

Inspect the existing cashback and bonus rules.

Reuse the actual approved expiry dates, eligibility requirements, usage limits and restrictions.

Do not invent new restrictions.

If a reward has expired, do not allow it to be redeemed.

If a bonus is restricted to certain services or campaigns, enforce those rules.

If the existing policy permits use on any Swiftvero shipping payment, allow it.

Do not allow cashback or bonus balances to become negative.

Redemption security

All reward redemption must be validated by the backend.

Use atomic transactions to prevent the same balance from being spent twice.

Deduct rewards only after the relevant payment or transaction is successfully confirmed according to the payment flow.

If payment fails, release any temporarily reserved reward balance.

Maintain a full transaction ledger.

Do not use frontend-only balance calculations.

Important accounting distinction

* Shipment credit is money the customer already paid.
* Cashback is a promotional reward.
* Bonus is a promotional reward.
* Outstanding balance is money still owed.

These must remain separate in the database and in the customer interface.

Do not silently convert one category into another.

